{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"uneducated-tinned-yapok","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\n`docs/event-schema.md` presents retired shell files as current writers and omits recognized event categories from its main contract. Ticket barky-suit-dial began the accepted documentation truth sweep but left historical shell names in the current table. F05 remains deferred, so this task must not add a generated catalog or parity gate.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Replace retired writer names with maintained producer seams.\n- Add `KEY_ADD` and `KEY_REVOKE` to the replayed event inventory.\n- Separate reducer-ignored sidecars from replay mutations.\n- Classify `PRECONDITIONS` and `SYNC` as recognized non-replay records.\n- Name the direct `BRIDGE_ALERT` producer.\n- Remove the deleted-writer footnote while preserving sidecar and compatibility semantics.\n- Run focused event-schema contracts and documentation checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every current writer entry names a maintained producer seam.\n- [ ] Replayed event types include `KEY_ADD` and `KEY_REVOKE`.\n- [ ] Reducer-ignored sidecars are distinct from replay mutations.\n- [ ] `PRECONDITIONS` and `SYNC` are classified as recognized non-replay records.\n- [ ] The direct `BRIDGE_ALERT` producer is named.\n- [ ] The deleted-writer footnote is absent.\n- [ ] No generated catalog or parity gate is added.\n- [ ] Focused event-schema and documentation checks pass.","id":"2b51-57f4-49ce-42c9","parent_id":"b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","accuracy","f31"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"F31 correct the event schema producer contract"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787512457993003001,"uuid":"84d74760-59ef-4dda-8d12-edf974e2696c"}